  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The framework is presented as a conceptual curriculum model based on the author's own teaching practice, without empirical evaluation of its long-term impact on K-12 classrooms.",
      "what": "This paper introduces the Critical Arts-Science-Advocacy Framework (CASAF), a three-part multidisciplinary learning sequence designed for K-12 teacher education and geography education. Developed from university-level teaching practice during the 2023–2025 school years, the framework guides students through mapping emotional geographies, conducting community science on campus biodiversity, and creating zines for public environmental storytelling.",
      "why": "It provides teacher educators with an actionable, non-traditional curriculum model that integrates arts-based research and environmental science, moving beyond standard science-only approaches to foster active Earth justice advocacy in future teachers."
